    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code and won't start. i looked at the manual but it's kind of confusing. can u tell me how to check the leak sensor and how to actually dry out the base of the machine properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An E15 error on a Bosch dishwasher typically indicates a leaked water level sensor issue, not necessarily a dry base, though condensation can trigger this. To check the sensor, ensure the unit is unplugged before gently pulling away sections of the outer panel to inspect the clean, gray water sensor located in the bottom tub housing. If the sensor is clogged or wet, use a bucket or squeegee to carefully remove standing water and a dry, lint-free cloth to pat it dry. Do not submerge the sensor in water, as this can damage the circuit board inside the machine. For the unit to start, the sensor must dry completely; if it remains faulty despite drying, you may need to replace the entire water sensor assembly. If you are uncomfortable performing these tasks or the error persists after basic drying, contact a qualified appliance technician for warranty assessment.",
